# XDRHelper

This is a template repository for creating new repositories. It includes a basic
structure for a code repository, including a README, LICENSE, and a CODE_OF_CONDUCT.

## Security Policy

When making contributions to this repository:

- Do not include any sensitive information in your code, commits, or pull requests.
- Do not store any passwords, API keys, tokens, or other sensitive information in the repository.
- Do not include any unnecessary information about DT Midstream, its employees, assets, or operations.


## Usage

To use this template, click the "Use this template" button at the top of the page.
Then, clone the repository to your local machine and start working on your project.


## Directory Structure

The repository is structured as follows:

- `.gitea/CONTRIBUTING.md`: Guidelines for contributing to the project.
- `.gitea/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md`: (very) Basic template for pull requests.
- `.gitea/ISSUE_TEMPLATE`: Directory containing Bug and Feature request issue templates. See https://docs.gitea.com/next/usage/issue-pull-request-templates for more info.
- `docs/`: Documentation for the project.
- `src/`: Source code for the project.
- `tests/`: Tests for the project.
- `LICENSE`: License file for the project.
- `README.md`: This file.
- `.gitignore`: Git ignore file that covers Windows OS, PowerShell, Python, and Dotnet Core.

All directories will have a single `.gitkeep` file to ensure they are included in the repository.